2026-09-27T09:27:24.3425080Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3425357Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3425758Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3426165Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3426301Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3426601Z ================
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3426781Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3427017Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3512139Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3512508Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3512682Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3513123Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3513382Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3513627Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3514291Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3515066Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3516159Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3516932Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3517092Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3517707Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3518478Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3518885Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3519345Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3519936Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3520199Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3520475Z ========
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3520627Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3522506Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3524702Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3525008Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3525678Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3526752Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3527629Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3528449Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3529077Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3529638Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3529794Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3530151Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3530364Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3531946Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3535184Z 
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3536416Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3537730Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:27:24.3538039Z 
